The problem asks us to simulate a process involving $N$ aliens over $N$ years.
Let $A_i$ be the initial number of stones the $i$-th alien has.
The $i$-th alien becomes an adult exactly $i$ years later.
When the $i$-th alien becomes an adult (at year $i$), every adult who has at least one stone gives exactly one stone to the $i$-th alien.
We need to find the number of stones each alien has after $N$ years.

Let's denote $C_i(t)$ as the number of stones the $i$-th alien has at year $t$.
Initially, at $t=0$, $C_i(0) = A_i$.
The aliens are indexed $1$ to $N$.
Alien $i$ becomes an adult at year $i$.
Before year $i$, alien $i$ is a minor.
At year $i$, alien $i$ becomes an adult.
